{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-ac918fffb45f739f", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# AudioMosaic: Contrastive Masked Audio Representation Learning\narXiv: 2605.14231\nAuthors: Hanxun Huang, Qizhou Wang, Xingjun Ma, Cihang Xie, Christopher Leckie, Sarah Erfani\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. AudioMosaic introduces a contrastive audio pre-training framework that uses structured time-frequency masking to construct complementary positive pairs for effective and efficient spectrogram-based learning.\n  2. A representation-level analysis using effective rank demonstrates that structured time-frequency masking prevents dimension collapse by reducing shared local redundancy between positive pairs.\n  3. AudioMosaic achieves state-of-the-art performance on multiple audio benchmarks, supports memory-efficient large-batch pre-training, and improves audio-language models when integrated as an audio encoder.\n\nTags: SSL, SSL/对比式", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f533bf06-cac2-4284-a5b9-fefe61b594df", "uuid": "1cf1d7a0-532b-45ca-b2c4-cc0f9032f021", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T06:07:16.458Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# AudioMosaic: Contrastive Masked Audio Representation Learning\narXiv: 2605.14231\nAuthors: Hanxun Huang, Qizhou Wang, Xingjun Ma, Cihang Xie, Christopher Leckie, Sarah Erfani\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. AudioMosaic introduces a contrastive audio pre-training framework that uses structured time-frequency masking to construct complementary positive pairs for effective and efficient spectrogram-based learning.\n  2. A representation-level analysis using effective rank demonstrates that structured time-frequency masking prevents dimension collapse by reducing shared local redundancy between positive pairs.\n  3. AudioMosaic achieves state-of-the-art performance on multiple audio benchmarks, supports memory-efficient large-batch pre-training, and improves audio-language models when integrated as an audio encoder.\n\nTags: SSL, SSL/对比式", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-9978691295898fa1", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# WavFlow: Audio Generation in Waveform Space\narXiv: 2605.18749\nAuthors: Feiyan Zhou, Luyuan Wang, Shoufa Chen, Zhe Wang, Zhiheng Liu, Yuren Cong, Xiaohui Zhang, Fanny Yang, Belinda Zeng\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavFlow introduces a simplified architecture that synthesizes high-fidelity audio directly in raw waveform space using waveform patchify, x-prediction flow matching, and specialized signal preprocessing to eliminate the need for audio tokenizers.\n  2. An automated data curation pipeline is developed to harvest large-scale, high-quality video-text-audio triplets to address the sensitivity of direct waveform modeling to data quality and scale.\n  3. Empirical validation demonstrates competitive results on VGGSound and AudioCaps benchmarks, proving that end-to-end raw waveform generation matches or exceeds the performance of established latent-based methods.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f533bf06-cac2-4284-a5b9-fefe61b594df", "uuid": "e65a2244-7a0a-441e-8a12-23f3e951660d", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T06:07:16.795Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# WavFlow: Audio Generation in Waveform Space\narXiv: 2605.18749\nAuthors: Feiyan Zhou, Luyuan Wang, Shoufa Chen, Zhe Wang, Zhiheng Liu, Yuren Cong, Xiaohui Zhang, Fanny Yang, Belinda Zeng\nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. WavFlow introduces a simplified architecture that synthesizes high-fidelity audio directly in raw waveform space using waveform patchify, x-prediction flow matching, and specialized signal preprocessing to eliminate the need for audio tokenizers.\n  2. An automated data curation pipeline is developed to harvest large-scale, high-quality video-text-audio triplets to address the sensitivity of direct waveform modeling to data quality and scale.\n  3. Empirical validation demonstrates competitive results on VGGSound and AudioCaps benchmarks, proving that end-to-end raw waveform generation matches or exceeds the performance of established latent-based methods.\n\nTags: TTS, TTS/架构-NAR-Flow", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8aec2a0759fbb838", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Kimi-Audio Technical Report\narXiv: 2504.18425\nAuthors: KimiTeam, Ding Ding, Zeqian Ju, Yichong Leng, Songxiang Liu, Tong Liu, Zeyu Shang, Kai Shen, Wei Song, Xu Tan, Heyi Tang, Zhengtao Wang, Chu Wei, Yifei Xin, Xinran Xu, Jianwei Yu, Yutao Zhang, Xinyu Zhou, Y. Charles, Jun Chen, Yanru Chen, Yulun Du, Weiran He, Zhenxing Hu, Guokun Lai, Qingcheng Li, Yangyang Liu, Weidong Sun, Jianzhou Wang, Yuzhi Wang, Yuefeng Wu, Yuxin Wu, Dongchao Yang, Hao Yang, Ying Yang, Zhilin Yang, Aoxiong Yin, Ruibin Yuan, Yutong Zhang, Zaida Zhou\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a universal, open-source audio foundation model (Kimi-Audio) that achieves state-of-the-art performance across audio understanding, generation, and speech conversation tasks within a single unified framework.\n  2. Design of a novel LLM architecture featuring continuous acoustic features as input and discrete semantic tokens as output, utilizing shared transformer layers with parallel dual-generation heads for text and audio.\n  3. Development of a chunk-wise streaming detokenizer based on flow matching, incorporating a training-free look-ahead mechanism to generate high-quality and low-latency audio waveforms.\n  4. Curation of a large-scale pre-training dataset comprising over 13 million hours of diverse audio data, processed via an automatic pipeline to generate high-quality, long-form annotations.\n  5. Construction of a cost-effective, diverse supervised fine-tuning dataset entirely from open-source data and processing tools, without relying on data purchases.\n  6. Design of a comprehensive continual pre-training strategy that initializes from a pre-trained text LLM and bridges the audio-text gap through unimodal, mapping, and interleaving pre-training tasks.\n  7. Creation and open-sourcing of a standardized evaluation toolkit that ensures fair and reproducible benchmarking of audio foundation models across diverse tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, TTS, LALM/对话型, LALM/理解型, LALM/音频标记-融合, TTS/功能-流式, LALM/对话型-并行生成", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f533bf06-cac2-4284-a5b9-fefe61b594df", "uuid": "3f200884-36b9-40da-87f6-db4df0e24eaa", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T06:07:17.089Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Kimi-Audio Technical Report\narXiv: 2504.18425\nAuthors: KimiTeam, Ding Ding, Zeqian Ju, Yichong Leng, Songxiang Liu, Tong Liu, Zeyu Shang, Kai Shen, Wei Song, Xu Tan, Heyi Tang, Zhengtao Wang, Chu Wei, Yifei Xin, Xinran Xu, Jianwei Yu, Yutao Zhang, Xinyu Zhou, Y. Charles, Jun Chen, Yanru Chen, Yulun Du, Weiran He, Zhenxing Hu, Guokun Lai, Qingcheng Li, Yangyang Liu, Weidong Sun, Jianzhou Wang, Yuzhi Wang, Yuefeng Wu, Yuxin Wu, Dongchao Yang, Hao Yang, Ying Yang, Zhilin Yang, Aoxiong Yin, Ruibin Yuan, Yutong Zhang, Zaida Zhou\nYear: 2025 | Venue: \nTopic: audio_understanding\nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. Introduction of a universal, open-source audio foundation model (Kimi-Audio) that achieves state-of-the-art performance across audio understanding, generation, and speech conversation tasks within a single unified framework.\n  2. Design of a novel LLM architecture featuring continuous acoustic features as input and discrete semantic tokens as output, utilizing shared transformer layers with parallel dual-generation heads for text and audio.\n  3. Development of a chunk-wise streaming detokenizer based on flow matching, incorporating a training-free look-ahead mechanism to generate high-quality and low-latency audio waveforms.\n  4. Curation of a large-scale pre-training dataset comprising over 13 million hours of diverse audio data, processed via an automatic pipeline to generate high-quality, long-form annotations.\n  5. Construction of a cost-effective, diverse supervised fine-tuning dataset entirely from open-source data and processing tools, without relying on data purchases.\n  6. Design of a comprehensive continual pre-training strategy that initializes from a pre-trained text LLM and bridges the audio-text gap through unimodal, mapping, and interleaving pre-training tasks.\n  7. Creation and open-sourcing of a standardized evaluation toolkit that ensures fair and reproducible benchmarking of audio foundation models across diverse tasks.\n\nTags: LALM, TTS, LALM/对话型, LALM/理解型, LALM/音频标记-融合, TTS/功能-流式, LALM/对话型-并行生成", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
