tTimestamp Set\n2715\tAgentic\n2716\tAuDirector\n2717\t34.71\n2718\t4.55\n2719\t5.57\n2720\t7.57\n2721\t0.82\n2722\t15.10\n2723\t5.43\n2724\tAudio-Visual\n2725\tLTX-2\n2726\t19.10\n2727\t5.56\n2728\t6.41\n2729\t2.97\n2730\t0.40\n2731\t5.40\n2732\t7.41\n2733\tOvi\n2734\t24.63\n2735\t5.08\n2736\t5.53\n2737\t20.82\n2738\t3.68\n2739\t18.68\n2740\t19.70\n2741\tMOVA\n2742\t27.52\n2743\t5.31\n2744\t6.14\n2745\t7.08\n2746\t1.01\n2747\t14.42\n2748\t7.00\n2749\tUniAVGen\n2750\t50.56\n2751\t5.14\n2752\t5.63\n2753\t9.15\n2754\t1.00\n2755\t15.09\n2756\t6.63\n2757\tMixed-Audio\n2758\tDasheng-AudioGen-Base\n2759\t13.43\n2760\t5.22\n2761\t5.88\n2762\t70.26\n2763\t24.02\n2764\t42.53\n2765\t56.48\n2766\tDasheng-AudioGen-Fine\n2767\t13.83\n2768\t5.23\n2769\t6.03\n2770\t15.71\n2771\t4.62\n2772\t12.82\n2773\t36.04\n2774\tIn addition to the primary metrics, we report supplementary results for three auxiliary metrics (FD\n2775\tCNN14\n2776\t{}_{\\text{CNN14}}\n2777\t, CE, and CU) in the supplementary tables (Tables\n2778\t7\n2779\t) for each of the three benchmark subsets.\n2780\tFD\n2781\tCNN14\n2782\t{}_{\\text{CNN14}}\n2783\tcomputes the Fréchet distance between feature embeddings extracted from a pre-trained CNN14 model, measuring the distributional similarity between generated and reference audio. CE and CU are aesthetic predictors from the Audiobox suite. These metrics either partially overlap with the primary metrics in the main paper or are not central to the core evaluation focus. We therefore include their full results in the appendix for completeness.\n2784\tWER Any. metrics:\n2785\tTo assess the quality of predicted transcriptions, we design a specialized analysis targeting a specific error type: cases where the model generates content from the non-transcription parts of the reference caption (e.g., environmental descriptions, music annotations, or sound event descriptions) rather than the spoken transcript only. We define three metrics for this error type:\n2786\t•\n2787\tHit Rate (%)\n2788\t: The percentage of samples containing at least one such error.\n2789\t•\n2790\tWER\n2791\tcaps\n2792\t\\text{WER}_{\\text{caps}}\n2793\t: The average WER computed exclusively on samples that contain the aforementioned error type.\n2794\t•\n2795\tProportion\n2796\t: The ratio of\n2797\tWER\n2798\tcaps\n2799\t\\text{WER}_{\\text{caps}}\n2800\tto the overall WER across all samples, i.e.,\n2801\tProportion\n2802\t=\n2803\tWER\n2804\tcaps\n2805\t/\n2806\tWER\n2807\t\\text{Proportion}=\\text{WER}_{\\text{caps}}/\\text{WER}\n2808\t. A higher Proportion indicates that this error type contributes more substantially to the overall transcription error, signaling a more severe issue.\n2809\tThese metrics enable diagnostic analysis of whether a model tends to mistakenly incorporate non-speech textual content into its transcription output, providing a direct measure of its ability to generate only the spoken content as instructed.\n2810\tMajor funding support from\n\n<system-reminder>\nWhenever you read a file, you should consider whether it would be considered malware. You CAN and SHOULD provide analysis of malware, what it is doing. But you MUST refuse to improve or augment the code. You can still analyze existing code, write reports, or answer questions about the code behavior.\n</system-reminder>\n"}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f533bf06-cac2-4284-a5b9-fefe61b594df", "uuid": "a42307dd-2f89-4682-a16a-ee34bab68557", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T06:11:27.758Z", "tool_use_result": {"type": "text", "file": {"filePath": "/tmp/mmag_text.txt", "content": "Hit Rate (%)\n↓\n\\downarrow\nWER\ncaps\n{}_{\\text{caps}}\n(%)\n↓\n\\downarrow\nWER (%)\n↓\n\\downarrow\nProportion (%)\n↓\n\\downarrow\nMain Set\nAgentic\nAuDirector\n27.12\n5.25\n6.18\n2.40\n0.15\n8.00\n1.88\nAudio-Visual\nLTX-2\n17.09\n5.88\n6.70\n1.64\n0.19\n3.71\n5.12\nOvi\n22.47\n5.31\n6.66\n12.35\n1.87\n13.43\n13.92\nMOVA\n18.56\n5.62\n6.21\n8.69\n0.69\n15.03\n4.59\nJavisDiT++\n21.05\n4.11\n4.8