{"type": "user", "message": {"role": "user", "content": [{"tool_use_id": "chatcmpl-tool-8344efc6b551472a", "type": "tool_result", "content": "# Dasheng AudioGen: A Unified Model for Generating Coherent Audio Scenes from Text\narXiv: 2605.27838\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Dasheng AudioGen, a unified text-to-audio framework that jointly generates intelligible speech, music, sound effects, and environmental acoustics within a single audio scene without domain-specific modeling.\n  2. We introduce structured multi-view captions, a layered design that provides fine-grained supervision and disentangled control over different audio components while remaining compatible with agentic systems.\n  3. We introduce a unified semantic-acoustic representation based on DashengTokenizer as the shared latent space, which provides semantic priors for efficient training and sufficient capacity to disentangle and fuse concurrent audio components.\n  4. We establish a comprehensive evaluation pipeline for audio scene generation, demonstrating that Dasheng AudioGen substantially outperforms expert pipelines in mixed-audio scenes while remaining competitive with specialized models.\n\nTags: method, experiments, we propose, we introduce", "is_error": false}]}, "parent_tool_use_id": null, "session_id": "f533bf06-cac2-4284-a5b9-fefe61b594df", "uuid": "a8dd8fe6-7e0e-45c0-8617-6d1d5a6fa503", "timestamp": "2026-08-10T06:14:06.003Z", "tool_use_result": {"stdout": "# Dasheng AudioGen: A Unified Model for Generating Coherent Audio Scenes from Text\narXiv: 2605.27838\nAuthors: \nYear: 2026 | Venue: \nTopic: \nStatus: unread\n\nContributions:\n  1. We propose Dasheng AudioGen, a unified text-to-audio framework that jointly generates intelligible speech, music, sound effects, and environmental acoustics within a single audio scene without domain-specific modeling.\n  2. We introduce structured multi-view captions, a layered design that provides fine-grained supervision and disentangled control over different audio components while remaining compatible with agentic systems.\n  3. We introduce a unified semantic-acoustic representation based on DashengTokenizer as the shared latent space, which provides semantic priors for efficient training and sufficient capacity to disentangle and fuse concurrent audio components.\n  4. We establish a comprehensive evaluation pipeline for audio scene generation, demonstrating that Dasheng AudioGen substantially outperforms expert pipelines in mixed-audio scenes while remaining competitive with specialized models.\n\nTags: method, experiments, we propose, we introduce", "stderr": "", "interrupted": false, "isImage": false, "noOutputExpected": false}}
